# Project rules

- Sunberry Hollow is a 2D top-down pixel-art RPG: 640x360 base resolution, 32 px tiles,
  nearest-neighbour filtering, pixel snapping on. Never rebuild it as 3D.
- Battlers are the literal dishes with their real culinary names (Berry Compote,
  Blackberry Tart, Hard-Boiled Egg, Fried Cauliflower). No food monsters, no humanoid or
  animal food, no fantasy species names.
- Chef level never blocks a recipe attempt. Only a recipe scroll grants 100% cooking
  success; unmastered attempts cap at 95%.
- Equipment access is separate from ownership (an NPC's fryer can be usable before owned).
- Cooking quality and a food's combat level are separate from chef level.
- Pixel art is generated procedurally by res://scripts/art.gd until real sprite sheets
  replace the individual builders.
